# The Haven's leaders, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): work, the news
# and what they make of you come out of talk. Each topic carries a built reply (call:slot:N): 0 the
# job (their own, else the stronghold's contracts), 1 the built news, 2 what they make of you.
# Voice: warm, worried, practical, darkly funny sideways. The List is said sideways, never announced.

conv haven.leader.work_food
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when need:food & !exiled
topic "Ask why the bowls are half full."
prio ask
voice haven

bind short = house:nearest_short

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? stronghold :: "The chair's table, and the soup on it is mostly a rumour. Every house is eating thinner than it says."
  say? trait:merciful :: "Sit down first. You look like the soup. Stores are low, love. Lower than we tell the children."
  say? trait:pragmatist :: "Food in, food out. Lately it's mostly out. I can do the sums. I'd rather not."
  say "Stores are down to the tins with no labels. We open one and find out what's for supper."
  say? bound:short :: "{bind:short} went to half portions. I can hear it from here, and it isn't close."
  say? night :: "And it's night, which is when people count what's left."
  say "We'll manage. We always say that. Mostly we do."
  > @who "Who's short, exactly?" -> who
  > @why "Why not ask Bastion for rations?" -> bastion
  > @worth "What's in it for me?" -> worth
  > @nurse "Who's eating least? It shows first." -> nurse   if bg:nurse,doctor,elder
  > @help "Is there something I can do?" -> offer
  > @no "Not today." -> hub

node who
  say? bound:short :: "{bind:short} first. Then the rest, one by one, like lights going off."
  say "Everyone. Some just say it louder."
  say? supply:lost :: "The last truck didn't come. Nobody's saying why, which means somebody knows."
  say "It's never the food that runs out first. It's the patience."
  > @help2 "Then let me help." -> offer
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node bastion
  say? truce:bastion :: "We've a truce with Bastion. A truce isn't a larder. They're counting their own tins."
  say? feud:bastion :: "Ask Bastion? They'd ask what's in it for them, then count us."
  say "They'd feed us for a list of names. We don't hand out lists."
  > @help3 "Then let me help." -> offer
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node worth
  say? trait:merciful :: "Supper. A bed. People who'll remember your face kindly. It's what we've got, and we give it all."
  say "Favor, a meal, and a name people say nicely. Don't laugh. Out here that's money."
  > @help4 "Fair. What's the job?" -> offer
  > @dry4 "Supper it is, then." -> offer   dry
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node nurse
  say "The old ones. They pass their bowls along when nobody's looking, and then they're the ones looking thin."
  say "You noticed. Most people only notice the children."
  > @help5 "Let me help with the food." -> offer
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node offer
  say? tier:haven>=trusted :: "I'd hoped you'd say that. I've a list. Of course I've a list."
  say "There's work. Not glamorous. It feeds people. See if it suits."
  > @take "Show me." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later "Let me think about it." -> hub

node other_route
  say "You're with another lot now. I heard. People still need feeding, whoever you march with."
  > @take2 "Is there still work?" -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node after
  say? cure_held:haven :: "We hold the cure, and the stores don't know it. People still eat every day."
  say "The cure's out, or near enough, and the soup hasn't heard. People still eat every day."
  > @take3 "Then I'll still work." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

conv haven.leader.work
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !need:food & !exiled
topic "Ask what's keeping them up."
prio ask
voice haven

bind over = news:overrun
bind burned = news:burned

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? need:security & bound:over :: "{bind:over} went to the dead. That's close enough to hear on a still night."
  say? need:security :: "The fences. Every house thinks its fence is fine until it isn't."
  say? need:people :: "Empty beds. We have more beds than people now, and that's never a good sign."
  say? need:supplies :: "Bandages boiled and boiled again. Batteries. Thread. The small things keep a house alive."
  say? bound:burned :: "{bind:burned} burned, and nobody put it out. Somebody will ask us to take them in."
  say "It's quiet. Quiet is when things go missing."
  say? rain :: "And the roof in the east room leaks. That's not the worst of it, only the loudest."
  say? finale:open :: "And everyone's picking a side for the cure, as if the soup will wait."
  say? trait:talker :: "I'd tell you the rest, but then you'd know as much as me, and I'd have nothing to trade."
  say "Same as always. Too many people need too many things."
  > @what "What happened there?" -> place   if bound:over
  > @burnt "Who's taking the burned-out families?" -> families   if bound:burned
  > @fences "Who's watching the fences?" -> fences
  > @elder "You've seen worse than this. Say it." -> told   if bg:elder
  > @press "Tell me what you're not saying." -> told | half | half   check persuade haven 2 easier:merciful harder:paranoid bg:elder,nurse
  > @help "Can I help?" -> offer

node place
  say "The dead came in through the gardens, the way they do. The people left by the front, the way we taught them."
  say "Some got to us. Some didn't. We read the names at supper."
  > @help2 "Then let me help." -> offer
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node families
  say "We are. Of course we are. Where else would they go. We'll squeeze."
  say "Squeezing is a skill. We've had a lot of practice."
  > @help3 "Let me help with that." -> offer
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node fences
  say? need:security :: "Children and old men, in shifts. They're good at shouting. Shouting isn't a fence."
  say "Whoever's awake. That's the rota. Being awake."
  > @help4 "I could take a shift of a kind." -> offer
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node told
  say? major:every_name :: "The council's arguing about the List again. Who's on it, who comes off. Every house has an opinion and a pencil."
  say "The council argues about who gets the next bed. It's not the arguing that keeps me up. It's that they're right, both of them."
  do learn:haven.council_argues:6h
  > @help5 "Then give me something useful to do." -> offer
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node half
  say "Nothing you'd sleep better for knowing. Ask me again when you've eaten here a few times."
  > @help6 "Then give me something to do." -> offer
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node offer
  say? trait:merciful :: "Eat first. Then work. That's the order here, whatever the council says."
  say "There's always something. Nobody comes to the Haven for the glamour."
  > @take "Show me." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later "Let me think about it." -> hub

node other_route
  say "You're walking with another lot now. Fine. People here still need things doing, whoever you march with."
  > @take2 "Is there still work?" -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

node after
  say "The cure's done, and people still fall off roofs and run out of thread. Grief has a lot of chores."
  > @take3 "Then I'll still work." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back7 "Something else." -> hub

conv haven.leader.news
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !exiled
topic "Ask what the houses are saying."
prio world
voice haven

bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by
bind from = news:taken_from
bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind horde = news:horde
bind hungry = news:hungry
bind gone = news:emptied
bind saved = news:rescue

node start
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:emptied -> emptied
  jump news:taken -> taken
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:rescue -> rescue
  jump news:hungry -> hungry
  say? epilogue :: "The houses are saying goodbye to each other. On the radio, in letters, in tins left on doorsteps."
  say? cure>=75 :: "The houses are saying the lab's close. Close is a word that's been close for weeks."
  say? outbreak:overrun :: "The houses are saying the roads are theirs now. The dead's, I mean. We go out in twos."
  say "The houses are saying what houses say. Who coughed, who's courting, who took the last of the jam."
  say? !night & hour<11 :: "Morning gossip's the kindest. People haven't slept on it yet."
  > @mine "And what are they saying about me?" -> me
  > @more "Anything else going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back0 "Something else." -> hub

node dead
  say "{bind:dead} is dead. We heard it from three houses before the radio said it, and the radio had it wrong."
  say? trait:merciful :: "Whoever they were to you, their name gets read tonight. We don't skip anyone."
  say "Whatever they were, they kept people alive. That earns a name read out."
  > @who2 "Who takes their place?" -> place
  > @more1 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node place
  say "Whoever stands up first and doesn't sit down. That's how it went last time. That's how it goes."
  > @more2 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node emptied
  say "The last of them left the house in {bind:gone}. Took the bear off the door and carried it."
  say "Somebody will paint it again on our doors here. We've a lot of bears now."
  > @where "Where did they go?" -> went
  > @more3 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node went
  say "Here. The next house over. Wherever has a bowl. We don't turn people from the door. That's the one rule we've kept."
  > @more4 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node taken
  say "They're saying {bind:who} took {bind:took} from {bind:from}. Fighting over a town nobody can live in."
  say? truce:redhand :: "We've a truce with the Red Hand, so I'm told to say nothing. I'm saying nothing very loudly."
  say "Whoever holds it, the families there still need feeding."
  > @true "Is that true?" -> sure
  > @more5 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node sure
  say "As true as anything said over soup. Someone's cousin saw the flag change. Cousins are reliable about flags."
  > @more6 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

node horde
  say "A crowd of them came through near {bind:horde}. Someone rang a bell, or ran a generator, and they came to see."
  say "Tell people: quiet is a kindness now. Noise is a dinner bell."
  > @more7 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back7 "Something else." -> hub

node rescue
  say "Someone brought people in alive at {bind:saved}. Alive. Every house heard it by supper."
  say? helped :: "Some say it was you. I didn't correct them."
  say "That's the good kind of gossip. We run short of it."
  > @more8 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back8 "Something else." -> hub

node hungry
  say "{bind:hungry} is on half portions. They say it isn't, which is how you know."
  say "The Haven doesn't blame. We send tins. When we have tins."
  > @more9 "What else is going round?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back9 "Something else." -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  jump best:haven -> me_known
  say? tier:haven>=trusted :: "That you're one of ours, near enough. That you eat with your hat off. Small things. They count."
  say? fresh :: "That there's a new face. People are always kind to a new face for a day or two. Use it."
  say "Not much yet. That's not a bad thing. The ones they talk about are mostly trouble or dead."
  > @back10 "Something else." -> hub

node me_known
  say "That you {best}. They say it at supper, with the bread. It's the best place to be said."
  > @back11 "Something else." -> hub

node me_colours
  say "That you came in wearing someone else's colours. People notice colours. They're polite about it. To your face."
  > @back12 "Something else." -> hub

conv haven.leader.me
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !exiled
topic "Ask if you're welcome here."
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  jump kit:other -> colours
  jump bite_shown -> bitten
  jump infamy:haven>=15 -> infamous
  jump tier:haven>=trusted -> trusted
  jump tier:haven>=known -> known
  say? fresh :: "A new face. You've the look of someone who's just been told the rules and is still deciding which ones count."
  say "Welcome's a big word. You're fed and you're inside. That's most of it."
  > @more "Where do I stand with you, honestly?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @fair "Fair enough." -> hub

node colours
  say? kit:full :: "Head to boot in someone else's kit, in my house. I'll assume you're cold and not lost."
  say "You're wearing their colours. We don't shoot through doors with bears on them. Don't make us reconsider."
  > @explain "It was what I could find." -> found
  > @more1 "Where do I stand with you?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node found
  say "Everything is. Take it off before supper, love. The children ask questions."
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node bitten
  say "Show me the arm. No. Don't. I can see it from here."
  say? declared :: "You told the house. That's why you're still inside. That's the whole of the rule."
  say "Tell the house before it tells us. That's the one thing we ask."
  > @more2 "Am I still welcome?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node infamous
  say? worst:haven :: "People here know you {worst}. They're polite about it. That's how you know it's serious."
  say "People go quiet when you come in. That's not a welcome. That's a habit we learned."
  > @more3 "Say it straight. Where do I stand?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node trusted
  say? best:haven :: "You {best}. You'll be welcome here when there's nothing left to welcome you with."
  say? title:haven :: "They call you {title:haven} in the houses. They don't call many people anything."
  say "You're one of the people I don't count the bowls against."
  > @more4 "Where do I stand, in full?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node known
  say? helped :: "You helped us. People remember who helped. We've no other way to pay."
  say? jobs:haven>=3 :: "You've done a few jobs for us. The houses have started saying your name without a question mark."
  say "You're known here. Known is good. Known means someone would notice if you didn't come back."
  > @more5 "And where do I stand?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub
